\cf0 You essentially have \'93Google APIs Explorer in a box\'94: 
\f3\fs26 embedded.js
\f0\fs24  renders the Explorer UI and 
\f3\fs26 codemirror_bin.js
\f0\fs24  gives you the JSON editor/pretty printer.explorer.apis.google+2\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Internal API scratchpad (beyond Google APIs)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use the embedded Explorer pattern as a generic \'93API workbench\'94 for your own REST endpoints.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Replace the base URLs/operations in a forked front-end so devs can pick an internal service, tweak JSON in a CodeMirror editor, and hit Execute with proper OAuth/JWT attached.stackoverflow+1 \
\ls16\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Persist request/response examples so teams get living docs, not static Swagger pages.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://research.google.com/pubs/archive/46675.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 research.google}} \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 2. On-page API docs with live console\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Drop this HTML (or a variant) directly into API documentation pages so readers can run the method in-place.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Use an 
\f3\fs26 <iframe>
\f0\fs24  pointing to your embedded Explorer host for each operation section; default the method, parameters, and scopes via query params or config in the host page.cloud.google+1 \
\ls17\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Capture the Explorer\'92s generated code samples (curl, Node, Python) and surface \'93copy-paste runnable\'94 snippets next to the docs.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developers.google.com/explorer-help/code-samples"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 developers.google}} \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Customer-facing \'93API tester\'94 portal\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Turn it into a safe sandbox where external integrators can experiment without touching Postman.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls18\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Gate the page behind Google OAuth or your IdP; scope it to only the publicly supported APIs and methods you want to expose.github+1 \
\ls18\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Pre-fill common scenarios (e.g., \'93list files\'94, \'93create object\'94) as saved templates that load into the CodeMirror editor with one click.developers.google+1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 4. QA / support debugging surface\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Let support and QA probe user issues by replaying calls visually.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls19\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Build a small UI that lets them paste a raw HTTP request or set a few toggles; map that into the Explorer\'92s request editor (CodeMirror) and execute it live against prod or a mirror environment.research.google+1 \
\ls19\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Store a history of executed calls per ticket so support can share exact repro steps with engineering.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://research.google.com/pubs/archive/46675.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 research.google}} \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Teaching / onboarding lab\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use it as the centerpiece for \'93learn this API in 30 minutes\'94 workshops.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls20\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Pre-configure a sequence of tasks: each step opens the Explorer with a specific method and partial parameters; learners fill in the blanks and run.developers.google+1 \
\ls20\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Pair it with the official client libraries (Node, Python, etc.) so learners can run an API call in Explorer, then copy the equivalent code and run it locally.googleapis+2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
